<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Serres</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Serres is a city in the region of Macedonia in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, in the fertile valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/struma">Strymon</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> took it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> in 1345, and after his death it became the seat of his widow Helena and of the despot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jovan-uglesa">Jovan Uglješa</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> captured it in 1383, and it was part of their empire until 1913.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/serres.jpg" alt="Serres" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Мико · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saints_Theodore_Tyro_and_Theodore_Stratelates_Church,_Serres_072.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
